Configurable sequential line-cache tile height in reducev.

reducev wraps a sequential input in a line cache whose tile_height sets the
strip height. Y accumulates within a strip and restarts at each boundary, so
the strip height decides which output rows land exactly on a phase tie and
which land a ULP below it. libvips uses 10; reproducing the Wix CDN requires
16.

The value is read from VIPS_TILE_HEIGHT at runtime and defaults to the
upstream 10, so an unpatched-looking build results when the variable is unset.

--- a/libvips/resample/reducev.cpp
+++ b/libvips/resample/reducev.cpp
@@ -1026,7 +1026,8 @@
 		g_info("reducev sequential line cache");
 
 		if (vips_sequential(in, &t[4],
-				"tile_height", 10,
+				"tile_height", g_getenv("VIPS_TILE_HEIGHT") ?
+					atoi(g_getenv("VIPS_TILE_HEIGHT")) : 10,
 				// "trace", TRUE,
 				nullptr))
 			return -1;
